Package: factomics
Title: One Toolbox for Multi-Omics Factor Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Bernard Isekah", "Osang'ir", , "bernard.osangir@sckcen.be",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A unified framework for multi-omics latent factor analysis.
    Runs several factor methods (PCA, Multiple Factor Analysis, FABIA, Group
    Factor Analysis, MOFA2, sparse generalised canonical correlation analysis,
    JIVE and the graph-guided robust adaptive-shrinkage Bayesian factor
    analysis of Zhang et al. (2024) <doi:10.1093/biomtc/ujad014>) through one consistent interface and returns their scores and
    loadings in a common format. Provides embeddings (PCA, UMAP, t-SNE),
    clustering with automatic choice of the number of clusters, method
    benchmarking, factor interpretation (variance explained, top loadings,
    covariate association), simulated data, and publication-ready plots.
